          <output>Stage 1 (&quot;Create Poem&quot;) of T00003_PoemTest_20260831T193409 completed as specified. The InstructionTask required creating/updating org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.Poem.bml with a fresh random German poem per execution. Execute produced exactly one model file: blocks/org/blockml/bml/workspace/playground/Poem.bml (currently untracked, hence the empty git diff; the whole playground/ dir shows as ??). The block is well-formed: FQN org.blockml.bml.workspace.playground.Poem, type playground:Poem, baseType core:Documentation, &lt;is> summary present. The &lt;documentation> element contains an original German poem of three four-line stanzas (&quot;Der Morgen legt sich grau ...&quot;), and &lt;properties> carry title=&quot;Der Morgen legt sich grau&quot;, author=&quot;John Doe&quot; (placeholder, consistent with prior poem runs), year=2026. The change is minimal and scoped to the single expected file; structure and conventions match the T00002 precedent. Execute did NOT modify any _meta/transform/ ModelTransformation files (the running/T00003 block reflects only the pre-existing stage-start commit). Note: `npx blockml validate` could not be run in this Reflect step (Bash disabled), so BML validity was not independently re-confirmed, but the file is well-formed XML consistent with surrounding definitions and ready for Stage 2 (&quot;Translate Poem&quot;).</output>
